From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haoze <haozegao0602@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:22:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] [shvla] iDMA backend: can_accept_transfer() also
 requires an empty regulation queue (fixes lost transfer / hbm_fill hang)

The regulation handler forwards a queued transfer (and only then sets current_transfer_size)
one cycle after enqueue_transfer(). In that window can_accept_transfer() still returned true,
the middle-end pushed the next line, and the first transfer was overwritten before its bursts
were issued: it is never read or acknowledged, so the DMA wait hangs. Seen as gemm1024_summa
(softhier.hbm_fill, 2 KiB rows) and siglip_encoder_layer. 283 of 1024 rows lost, exactly those
queued at regulation_queue depth = 1. Deeploy's backend (no regulation queue) passes the
same ELF. Carried in soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch and in the patched pulp working tree
(pulp/pulp/idma/be/idma_be.cpp); the hunk applies to the nested pulp HEAD without offset or fuzz.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
